  S~S  SimpleSal template documents: RELEASE

=====================

------------------------------------------ [delete after copying template]

    A description of the content or changes included in THIS VERSION

            tagged as a coherent collection of files in a repository of:

        [edit: SimpleSal App software, or, SimpleSal software]

    A repository is only a vessel for managing a blob of content that changes over Time, as a blob.
    Version control tasks need a bridge between the software content and the managed object containing it.

    In the software content context, nobody cares about the repository blob.
    In the repository content context, nobody cares about the software content.

    The RELEASE document for each collection of coherent content inside a blob is that bridge.

------------------------------------------

=====================

------------------------------------------

SimpleSal software component RELEASE Note Style Guide [delete after copying template]

------------------------------------------

     Each formal publication of a labeled version of software will describe the changes here.
     The content here is prepended to the official accumulation of all RELEASE files: CHANGELOG

     As stated above, the content is the bridge between the software content and the repository.
        repository-based change documentation : correlate repository activities to a labeled version
        source file-based change documentation : describe for a developer the software changes made

------------------------------------------

    Each repository will have an instance of RELEASE, which willl change with each release.

------------------------------------------

    The sequential numbering system chosen to identify unique versions is "the date of release".
    For the purposes of human discussion of features and complaints, a human version is used also.

------------------------------------------

